---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="About — Headaches & Heartbeats"
			description="Who is writing this, why, and what happened to them."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<article>
				<h1>About</h1>
				<hr />
				<div class="prose">
					<p>
						In [year], I got a viral illness. I recovered — or I thought I did. Several weeks later, I noticed things weren't right. My heart rate was higher than it should be. I was getting headaches I'd never had before. Simple things left me exhausted in a way that didn't match the effort involved.
					</p>
					<p>
						After various tests and referrals, I ended up with a diagnosis of <strong>post-viral dysautonomia</strong> — a dysfunction of the autonomic nervous system triggered by infection. It sits within a wider cluster of post-viral conditions that include ME/CFS and Long COVID, and shares features with POTS (postural orthostatic tachycardia syndrome).
					</p>
					<p>
						I'm not a clinician. I'm someone who, faced with a poorly-understood condition and a healthcare system under enormous pressure, decided to do what I could with what I had: document everything carefully, read the evidence honestly, test things systematically, and share what I find.
					</p>
					<h2>Why this site</h2>
					<p>
						When I was first trying to understand what was happening to me, I found a lot of anecdote, a lot of forum posts, and not much in the way of careful first-person accounts that took the evidence seriously. I wanted to create the kind of resource I was looking for: dispassionate, data-aware, honest about uncertainty.
					</p>
					<p>
						I write about specific interventions I'm trying — always with a description of the evidence, an account of my own experience, and data where I have it. I write evidence reviews of the research. I've built interactive versions of clinical questionnaires that are hard to find online. And I write about navigating the NHS, which has its own particular challenges.
					</p>
					<h2>What this site is not</h2>
					<p>
						This is not medical advice. Nothing here should be taken as a recommendation to try anything. I'm one person describing one experience of one condition. What applies to me may not apply to you, and any changes to treatment or management should be discussed with a doctor.
					</p>
					<p>
						I'm also not selling anything. The tools are free. I don't have a supplement line. I'm not affiliated with any device manufacturer (though I'll note when I've received anything for free). If I have an affiliate arrangement I'll disclose it clearly — and I'll also tell you when something doesn't work.
					</p>
					<h2>Contact</h2>
					<p>
						I'm not currently running a contact form. If you want to get in touch, the best route for now is to join the conversation wherever I share content.
					</p>

					<div class="disclaimer">
						<strong>Reminder:</strong> I'm a patient, not a clinician. Everything here reflects my personal experience and my reading of the evidence. Please discuss any medical decisions with your own doctor.
					</div>
				</div>
			</article>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
